	(no_connect (at 388.62 198.12) (uuid "42ed248f-6958-4630-bf27-35064cfb71cb"))
	(text "Lower monitor U_BQ1, BQ7695202. Local reference and exposed pad are CELL0.\nCell filter copied from SLUSE13B 7.3 and EVM guide section 5.4 Figure 5-9:\n20 ohm in series with each VC pin, 220 nF between adjacent filtered nodes, and 220 nF from the VC0 node to local VSS.\nSection 7.3 allows 20-100 ohm and 0.1-1 uF. Cell-resistor footprint and power rating are OPEN.\nVC pins are also the internal balance pins (Table 6-1). Host balancing is the firmware mode.\nExternal balance network is OPEN. R_B1-R_B33 stay fixed for the case and are not drawn.\nThose 33 resistors are not a 33-cell stack.\nBQ7695202 REG1 defaults to 3.3 V (section 5). That default does not replace REG0 or the wake pins.\nREG18 capacitor is 2.2 uF, inside the 1.8-22 uF range in section 7.10. REG1 capacitor is 1 uF (section 7.12).\nREGIN capacitor is 22 nF (section 7.11, allowed 15-27 nF). CBREG 150 pF is the table maximum, not a fitted part.\nBAT 100 ohm, 1 uF, and 100 pF follow Figure 16-2. High-voltage footprints are OPEN.\nCP1 is tied to BAT because the charge pump is unused (Table 16-3). Enabling it with that tie adds about 200 uA.\nCHG, DSG, PCHG, and PDSG are left floating (Table 16-3). Discharge protection is out of scope.\nFUSE and REG2 are left floating (Table 16-3). Pins 19 and 44 are not connected to silicon.\nPACK uses 10 kOhm to this monitor's top of stack, the no-high-side-FET connection in section 16.2.\nRST_SHUT, TS2, and LD wake sources are sheet ports marked OPEN. Do not put a thermistor on TS2 (section 13.5).\nSSZT191: every monitor needs a wake path. TS2 is pulled to this domain's VSS to wake; LD voltage must stay inside section 7.3.\nCRC I2C at 100 kHz. SDA is ESP32 GPIO21 and SCL is GPIO20. Startup 7-bit address is 0x08. Firmware then moves this device to 0x10.\nSRP and SRN are one Kelvin pair for the charge shunt. Place the 100 ohm / 100 nF filter at the device (SLUSE13B 16.2 and 18.1). Optional 100 pF and 0.1 uF-to-VSS parts are not fitted. Charging current must make SRP positive relative to SRN. CHG- is a sheet port.\nConnector value labels are wrong. These are assigned PCB nets, not harness proof, and no connector is relabeled here.\nJ_CELL1 pins 1-10 = CELL9 down to CELL0. J_CELL2 pins 1-9 = CELL18 down to CELL10.\nJ_CELL3 pins 1-8 = CELL26 down to CELL19. J_CELL4 pins 1-6 = CELL32 down to CELL27.\nPin 49 is the exposed pad of footprint TQFP-48-1EP and is tied to the local reference.\nSLUSE13B package outline PFB0048A shows no exposed thermal pad. Pad 49 keeps that footprint copper on the local reference.\nOPEN parts:\nD1: BAT series diode. MPN, voltage rating, and footprint are OPEN. Separate from the REG0 collector diode (SLUSE13B 16.2).\nQ1: REG0 NPN. MPN and footprint are OPEN. Collector-emitter must tolerate this monitor's own stack, not the full 32s pack.\nD2: REG0 collector diode. MPN, voltage rating, and footprint are OPEN.\nR19: BREG-to-VSS resistor. SLUSE13B 16.2.2 says a large resistor such as 10 MOhm; the value is not otherwise fixed.\nR20: SDA pull-up to this domain's REG1. Resistance is OPEN; the bus is 100 kHz and the capacitance is not yet fixed.\nR21: SCL pull-up to this domain's REG1. Resistance is OPEN.\nR23: RST_SHUT pulldown to local VSS. SLUSE13B 12.6 requires the pin low in normal operation; the resistor value is not specified. The upstream driver is the sheet port.\nR24: LD series resistor. Value, MPN, and footprint are OPEN. SSZT191 allows wake from LD only with the voltage limited to the datasheet range versus this domain's VSS.\nR_SH: Single charge-current shunt. Value, MPN, and footprint are OPEN. Do not copy the R001 silkscreen and do not put the existing shunt footprints in series.\nR27: TS1 series resistor. Firmware subtracts 500 ohm; the fitted value is OPEN.\nRT1: TS1 NTC. Value and MPN are OPEN. Firmware assumes 10 kOhm, beta 3380, and the internal 18 kOhm pull-up.\nR28: TS3 series resistor. Firmware subtracts 500 ohm; the fitted value is OPEN.\nRT2: TS3 NTC. Value and MPN are OPEN. Firmware assumes 10 kOhm, beta 3380, and the internal 18 kOhm pull-up.\nR29: ALERT series resistor. Firmware subtracts 500 ohm; the fitted value is OPEN.\nRT3: ALERT NTC. Value and MPN are OPEN. Firmware assumes 10 kOhm, beta 3380, and the internal 18 kOhm pull-up.\nR30: DCHG series resistor. Firmware subtracts 500 ohm; the fitted value is OPEN.\nRT4: DCHG NTC. Value and MPN are OPEN. Firmware assumes 10 kOhm, beta 3380, and the internal 18 kOhm pull-up.\nR31: HDQ series resistor. Firmware subtracts 500 ohm; the fitted value is OPEN.\nRT5: HDQ NTC. Value and MPN are OPEN. Firmware assumes 10 kOhm, beta 3380, and the internal 18 kOhm pull-up."
